{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/147367-compromise-conditions","id":147367,"title":"Compromise Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-23T18:04:02-07:00","id":147367,"title":"Compromise Conditions","content":"I felt that the use of the Guilty, Shaken, and especially Spooked Conditions for success on Compromise rolls was serviceable but lacked a certain thematic punch, and felt that it could use some more splat-specific Conditions for such. I came up with three new Conditions to replace them: Fixated, Jarred, and Exposed, roughly equivalent to Guilty, Shaken, and Spooked respectively. Let me know what you think!<br /> <br /> <b>Condition: Fixated</b><br /> <br /> Your character cannot stop thinking about their past actions and their consequences, though instead of overcome with a sense of guilt, one wonders about the ramifications and whether or not it could have been different if they had approached it from a different angle. Your character second guesses their decision constantly, and has a need to vocalize this self-doubt. So long as it is suppressed, it weighs upon everything they do. Your character suffers -2 dice penalty to any and all Extended Actions, as they require your concentration and focus.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Resolution: </b>Your character confesses their doubts and risks themselves or the mission to correct their perceived wrongs, make up for the previous mistake, or recognize their limitations, by choosing to automatically fail a related roll.<br /> </div> <br /> <b>Condition: Jarred</b><br /> <br /> The Unchained are already alien to reality, and your character's perceptions have grown out of sync with the external world around them, revealed as purely subjective by the consequences of their Compromise. Everything seems unreal or symbolic of larger occult matrices, and the influence of the God Machine can be seen in everything. They focus on the most minute of details and can see connections where they do not truly exist. While under the effects of this Condition, this tunnel vision and asynchronous perception of reality inflicts a -2 penalty to all Perception rolls.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Resolution:</b> Your character recognizes they are missing the forest for the trees, often through a rude awakening, represented by choosing to fail a Perception roll as above, or an Investigation, Empathy, or Occult roll.<br /> </div> <br /> <b>Condition: Exposed</b><br /> <br /> The Cover provides a bulwark against supernatural influence, but the connection between it and the demon within can seem tenuous at best. Though your character has resisted compromising the Cover, the distance between it and the demon seems all the more clear. It is more difficult for the demon to relate through and control its mental faculties, leaving it susceptible to outside influence. Your character has one less Door to resist social maneuvering with, and suffers a -2 dice penalty to resist supernatural influence.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Resolution: </b>Your character is shocked back into self-identity after opting to fail or give into social or supernatural influence, showing just how far they have drifted from the core perception of the Cover.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3058-juvenaliansatyr","name":"JuvenalianSatyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3058_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T17:28:10-07:00","id":150908,"title":"","content":"I like these <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Although I always hunger for more conditions to add to my repertoire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T02:36:40-08:00","id":834903,"title":"","content":"Necro, but these are extremely awesome and everything I've been looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}